  "lineage": "Brazilian late-1960s art-pop counter-cultural movement (1967-1969 peak) emerging in Salvador-Bahia-and-São-Paulo as fusion of bossa-nova harmonic-sophistication, Northeast forró-and-baião rhythmic-vocabulary, Anglo-American psychedelic-rock instrumentation (electric-guitar, fuzz, distortion), Stockhausen-and-Cage avant-garde electroacoustic-experimentation, and Brazilian-modernist-poetry pau-brasil concrete-and-anthropophagic literary-aesthetic. Built politically in opposition to the 1964-1985 Brazilian military dictatorship through ironic-pop subversion. The canonical recordings of the late-1960s tropicália phase shaped Brazilian-mainstream MPB 1970s-onward and influenced global art-rock through the 1990s-onward Western re-discovery wave.",
